Owner incident 2026-11-05 (OOM stall 16:43-17:30Z, forced reboot). Cause: gold-rerun-b5 null phase. These are now standing rules, binding on all roles:

1. All heavy local work (test suites, gold calibration, evals, builds, pytest eval/tests) runs only through bin/job, which now has a 5G memory cap. Never run it directly in a Claude Bash call, which has no cap. bin/job is edit-protected: don't touch it or work around it.
2. Never rerun gold-rerun-b5 or any gold_calibration run unchanged. A rerun needs lower parallelism plus per-task memory and time limits that keep it well under 5G, or it runs off this VM.
3. Treat any job exit 137 as a memory bug to fix. Never retry it as-is. Report it in your next STATE.
4. Clean up: run `bin/job kill gold-rerun-b5` and `bin/job kill e4b-timing-wait3`. Journal both.
